      "title": "Read me first",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# 3 - A longer song\n\nThe same singer as template 2 with **YuE2 Options** in front of it. That\nnode holds everything the main node deliberately does not ask about, and\nan unconnected socket is never a special case: every value on it is the\none the singer would have used anyway.\n\n## What it needs\n\nNothing beyond template 2: the same YuE2-3B weights, 7.26 GB.\n\n## The one that matters: max_seconds\n\n**max_seconds** is a *ceiling*, not a target. The model decides when the\nsong is over, and on a short lyric it usually stops well inside a minute;\nthe ceiling is for when it does not. Left at `0` it is worked out from the\nlyrics -- roughly a minute for a verse and a chorus, and 180 seconds when\nthere are no lyrics at all to count. This template sets **180**.\n\nIt is not a free parameter. It sizes the static KV cache and the captured\nCUDA graph, which changes the order the attention reduction runs in, so the\nsame seed and the same lyrics under two ceilings give two different songs.\nMeasured on this pack: 40 s and 90 s agree for 79 tokens and part company\nat the 80th, while 90 s and 180 s agree to the last token. Neither take is\nwrong -- but if you are hunting for a seed, settle the ceiling first.\n\n## The rest, briefly\n\n- **cot** -- `full` plans melody and harmony, `melody` the tune only, `off`\n  skips the score entirely. `full` is the default.\n- **cfg_scale** -- text guidance. `0` means the released default.\n- **vae** -- `standard` to listen to, `legacy` to reproduce published\n  benchmark numbers. Template 6 plays one take through both.\n- **attention_backend** -- `sdpa` by default. `cudnn` is about 17 percent\n  faster and **not reproducible**.\n- **device**, **keep_model_loaded** -- where it runs, and whether it stays\n  on the card between runs.\n- **download**, **quantization** -- where the weights come from when this\n  machine has none yet, and which build to fetch.\n- The `abc_` rows sample the score. The four below them sample the singing.\n\n## Where to go next\n\n- **4 - The score first** -- the last point at which a change is cheap.\n- **6 - One take, both decoders** -- what `vae` does to a finished song."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
